# 🔬 Multi-Agent Research Intelligence Synthesizer

![Streamlit](https://img.shields.io/badge/Streamlit-FF4B4B?style=for-the-badge&logo=Streamlit&logoColor=white)
![LangGraph](https://img.shields.io/badge/LangGraph-000000?style=for-the-badge&logo=python&logoColor=white)
![Groq](https://img.shields.io/badge/Groq-F55036?style=for-the-badge&logo=groq&logoColor=white)
![LangChain](https://img.shields.io/badge/LangChain-1C3C3C?style=for-the-badge&logo=chainlink&logoColor=white)
![Tavily](https://img.shields.io/badge/Tavily-0052CC?style=for-the-badge&logo=searchengineland&logoColor=white)

An intelligent, multi-agent research synthesis application powered by **LangGraph**, **Groq**, and **Streamlit**.

This system autonomously researches, plans, and synthesizes high-quality technical research reports. By breaking down the research process into specialized agentic roles — **Router**, **Researcher**, **Orchestrator**, and **parallel Workers** — it ensures well-structured, factually grounded, and citation-backed content.

---

## 🧠 Architecture & Workflow

The core intelligence is driven by a state machine built with **LangGraph**. The graph conditionally routes through research or directly to planning, then fans out tasks to parallel worker agents before reducing everything into a final polished report.

```mermaid
graph TD
    START((Start)) --> R[Router Node]
    R -->|Open Book / Hybrid| RES[Research Node<br/><i>Tavily Search</i>]
    R -->|Closed Book| O[Orchestrator Node]
    RES --> O
    O -->|Fan-Out Parallel Tasks| W[Worker Nodes]
    W --> RED[Reducer Subgraph<br/><i>merge_content</i>]
    RED --> END((End))
```

### 1. 🧭 Router Node
Analyzes the user's topic and decides the research mode:
- **Closed Book** — Evergreen concepts that don't need external research (recency window: ~10 years).
- **Hybrid** — Topics benefiting from up-to-date tools/models/examples (recency window: 45 days).
- **Open Book** — Highly volatile topics like news, pricing, or recent announcements (recency window: 7 days).

### 2. 🔎 Research Node (Tavily)
If research is needed, this node dispatches up to 3 targeted search queries to the **Tavily Search API**, fetches high-signal web results, deduplicates by URL, enforces recency filtering for `open_book` mode, and caps snippet sizes to stay within LLM token limits.

### 3. 🗂️ Orchestrator Node
Acts as the Senior Technical Editor. It takes the topic and gathered evidence, and designs a comprehensive **Plan** with 5–9 specific sections — each with a target word count, goal, bullet points, and citation/code requirements.

### 4. ⚙️ Worker Nodes (Parallel Fan-out)
Multiple worker agents run **in parallel** via LangGraph's `Send` API, each responsible for writing a single section defined by the Orchestrator. Workers strictly follow formatting constraints and cite evidence URLs to prevent hallucinations.

### 5. 🔀 Reducer Subgraph
Gathers all parallel-generated sections, sorts them into the correct order by section ID, and merges them into a single cohesive final Markdown report.

---

## ✨ Features

- **Multi-Agent Parallelism** — Sections are generated concurrently via LangGraph's fan-out (`Send`) for fast report creation.
- **Intelligent Routing** — Automatic detection of research mode (`closed_book` / `hybrid` / `open_book`) based on topic analysis.
- **Web-Grounded Research** — Tavily integration fetches authoritative, up-to-date sources for research-required topics.
- **Hallucination Mitigation** — Workers are instructed to only cite provided evidence URLs; unsupported claims are explicitly flagged.
- **Live Streaming UI** — Watch the LangGraph execution in real-time with per-node status updates and a live progress summary.
- **Structured Plan View** — Inspect the full Orchestrator plan as a dataframe before reading the final report.
- **Evidence Inspector** — Browse all retrieved web sources with titles, dates, and URLs in a dedicated tab.
- **Markdown Download** — Download the final synthesized report as a `.md` file with a single click.
- **Cloud-Ready** — No local file I/O; fully compatible with Streamlit Community Cloud.

---

## 🛠️ Setup & Installation

**1. Clone the repository**
```bash
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd Multi_Agent_Research
```

**2. Install dependencies**
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

**3. Configure Environment Variables**

Create a `.env` file in the root directory and add your API keys:
```ini
# Required: Primary LLM (Router + Orchestrator)
GROQ_API_KEY="your_groq_api_key_here"

# Optional: Secondary LLM for Workers (falls back to GROQ_API_KEY if not set)
GROQ_API_KEY_2="your_second_groq_api_key_here"

# Optional but recommended: enables web research for hybrid/open_book topics
TAVILY_API_KEY="your_tavily_api_key_here"

# Optional: override default models
GROQ_MODEL_1="openai/gpt-oss-20b"
GROQ_MODEL_2="openai/gpt-oss-20b"
```

> **Note**: Without a `TAVILY_API_KEY`, the system still works in `closed_book` mode. Research-required topics will return empty evidence.

---

## 💻 Usage

**Run the Streamlit app:**
```bash
streamlit run frontend.py
```

1. Enter your research **Topic** in the sidebar text area.
2. Select an **As-of date** to set the recency context.
3. Click **🚀 Generate Report**.
4. Monitor the live execution logs and progress JSON as each agent node runs.
5. Review the generated **Plan** (section breakdown), **Evidence** (web sources), and **Markdown Preview** in their respective tabs.
6. Download your final report using the **⬇️ Download Report (Markdown)** button.

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
Multi_Agent_Research/
├── backend.py          # LangGraph graph: all agent nodes, state schema, graph wiring
├── frontend.py         # Streamlit UI: streaming, tabs (Plan, Evidence, Preview, Logs)
├── requirements.txt    # Python dependencies
└── .env                # API keys (not committed)
```

---

## 🔑 Key Dependencies

| Package | Role |
|---|---|
| `langgraph` | State machine orchestration, fan-out (`Send`), subgraph support |
| `langchain-groq` | Groq LLM client (Router, Orchestrator, Workers) |
| `langchain-community` | Tavily search tool integration |
| `langchain-core` | Message types (`SystemMessage`, `HumanMessage`) |
| `pydantic` | Structured output schemas (`Plan`, `Task`, `EvidenceItem`) |
| `streamlit` | Interactive web UI with live streaming |
| `pandas` | Plan & evidence table rendering |
| `python-dotenv` | `.env` file loading |

